{
  "id": "COMPOUND:31863 - PROTEIN:5777",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between Npc191948 and SF-188 through a series of molecular targets. Npc191948 is implicated in targeting the 26S proteasome non-ATPase regulatory subunit 14, which is a known target of WS-5995 B. This compound further targets 5alpha,6alpha-Epoxy(22e,24r)-ergosta-8(14),22-dien-3beta,7alpha-diol, which in turn has SF-188 as its target. This pathway indicates a multi-step interaction where Npc191948 may influence SF-188 through the modulation of a proteasome-related molecule. Additionally, Npc191948 is also linked to Ataxin-2, which is targeted by a complex epoxy compound that also affects SF-188. These findings suggest that Npc191948 may exert its effects via a proteasome-related mechanism, potentially influencing SF-188 through the regulation of a specific protein. The evidence supports a mechanistic link between Npc191948 and SF-188, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
